            <div class="mb-16">
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-2">Comprehensive website audits and analysis</h2>
        <div class="h-1 w-16 bg-service-optimisation rounded-full mb-6" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none">
          <p class="text-lg mb-6">Before making changes, it's essential to understand what's actually holding a site back. Comprehensive audits combine analytics data, user behaviour patterns, and technical performance metrics to identify specific problems affecting results.</p>
          <p class="text-lg">This includes examining where users drop off, which pages load slowly, where navigation confuses visitors, and how mobile users experience the site differently. Real user data reveals patterns that assumptions miss, ensuring improvements target actual problems rather than perceived ones.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      
      <div class="mb-16">
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-2">UX improvements that reduce friction</h2>
        <div class="h-1 w-16 bg-service-optimisation rounded-full mb-6" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none">
          <p class="text-lg mb-6">Small changes to layout, navigation, and interaction patterns can dramatically improve how users engage with your site. Professional UX refinement focuses on reducing friction in key user journeys, making information easier to find, and ensuring design choices support rather than hinder your business goals.</p>
          <p class="text-lg">This might mean restructuring navigation to match how users actually search for information, improving call-to-action visibility and clarity, streamlining forms to reduce abandonment, or reorganising content hierarchy to highlight what matters most. Every refinement is guided by data and tested to ensure it genuinely improves the user experience and drives conversions.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      
      <div class="mb-16">
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-2">Core Web Vitals and page speed optimisation</h2>
        <div class="h-1 w-16 bg-service-optimisation rounded-full mb-6" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none">
          <p class="text-lg mb-6">Page speed directly impacts both user experience and search engine rankings. Slow websites frustrate visitors and get penalised by Google. Targeted performance optimisations make measurable improvements to loading times and Core Web Vitals scores — the metrics Google uses to rank websites.</p>
          <p class="text-lg">This includes optimising image formats and delivery, implementing effective caching strategies, removing unnecessary code and scripts, lazy loading content below the fold, and minifying CSS and JavaScript. The goal is faster loading times across all devices, particularly mobile, where performance matters most for both user satisfaction and SEO.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      
      <div class="mb-16">
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-2">Turn insights into results</h2>
        <div class="h-1 w-16 bg-service-optimisation rounded-full mb-6" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none">
          <p class="text-lg mb-6">Optimisation isn't about making arbitrary changes - it's about measurable improvements that support your business goals. Whether that means increasing conversions, reducing bounce rates, improving search rankings, or making content management easier for your team.</p>
          <p class="text-lg">You'll see clear before-and-after metrics showing exactly how improvements have impacted performance. Recent optimisation projects have delivered significant improvements in site speed, user engagement, and business metrics, all achieved through systematic analysis and targeted refinements rather than complete rebuilds.</p>
        </div>
